    [
      "heading",
      2,
      "result-and-persistence",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Result and persistence"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "UNetbootin extracts files and installs boot files on the selected filesystem, creating file-based live media rather than performing a raw image write or a MiniOS Installer deployment. Its use does not guarantee FAT32 formatting, EFI support, or persistence."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Persistence is enabled only when a boot entry or kernel command line requests it, and it still requires suitable writable storage. See "
        ],
        [
          "link",
          "/configuration/Boot-Modes.md",
          null,
          [
            [
              "text",
              "Boot modes"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "link",
          "/configuration/Initrd-Persistence.md",
          null,
          [
            [
              "text",
              "Initrd persistence"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " before relying on saved changes."
        ]
      ]
    ]
  ],
  "plain_text": "Using UNetbootin\nUNetbootin is a cross-platform open-source utility that allows you to create bootable USB drives for various Linux distributions, including MiniOS.\nImportant\nWarning: Incorrect device selection will result in data loss! Always double-check the selected drive and backup important data.\nDrive Requirements\nDrive Size\nSee Hardware Compatibility Guide for detailed system requirements and drive sizes.\nInstalling UNetbootin\nDownload UNetbootin from the official website\nInstall the program on your system:\nWindows: Run the installer as administrator\nLinux: Install from repository or use AppImage\nmacOS: Drag the application to the Applications folder\nCreating Bootable USB Drive\nLaunch UNetbootin as administrator/root\nSelect image source:\nSet the toggle to \"Disk image\"\nClick the \"...\" button and select the MiniOS ISO file\nSelect target device:\nIn the \"Drive\" list, select your USB drive\nEnsure the correct device is selected\nStart the process: Click \"OK\"\nWait for completion - the process may take 10-20 minutes\nResult and persistence\nUNetbootin extracts files and installs boot files on the selected filesystem, creating file-based live media rather than performing a raw image write or a MiniOS Installer deployment. Its use does not guarantee FAT32 formatting, EFI support, or persistence.\nPersistence is enabled only when a boot entry or kernel command line requests it, and it still requires suitable writable storage. See Boot modes and Initrd persistence before relying on saved changes.",
  "product_kind": "minios-markup-document",
  "schema_version": 1
}
